-- MIM iPad Inspector App — Figma reconciliation localization seed
-- Sponsor authorization: SPONSOR_DECISIONS_AND_IMPLEMENTATION_AUTHORIZATION.md, DEC-H
-- ('implement all Arabic/English keys now; the 94 flagged translations remain
-- marked for legal/native review but do not block development').
--
-- Namespace: keys use a deliberate 'figma.<page>.<string_id>' staging prefix,
-- NOT the app's real screen namespaces (field.*, f360.*, admin.*) — the actual
-- wizard/report-family screens these strings belong to are not yet built
-- (blocked on DEC-A/DEC-A-derived slices). Renaming to real in-code keys happens
-- as each screen is implemented; this migration only guarantees the Arabic/English
-- content exists and is traceable back to TRANSLATION_REVIEW_REGISTER.csv string_id.
--
-- 347 of 389 rows seeded (skipped 42 NON_PRODUCT_REFERENCE /
-- sample-data rows — those are placeholder/BRD-sample values, never user-visible copy).
-- ALL rows land as status='draft': the 94 HUMAN_DECISION_REQUIRED rows (legal/domain
-- terminology, see TRANSLATION_REVIEW_REGISTER.csv open_question_ids) are additionally
-- marked in the context column so the localization admin UI surfaces them for the
-- combined native-Arabic/legal review pass (DEC-H).
-- Paste-safe: straight ASCII quotes and Arabic text only, no smart quotes.

on conflict (key) do update
  set ar = excluded.ar, en = excluded.en, context = excluded.context
  where ui_strings.status = 'draft';   -- never clobber a human-reviewed translation
